Phased roadmap
Phase A — Codebase inventory (reuse before building) ← START HERE

Antigravity poora codebase scan kare (dev-theme-peri, theme-engine/components, base-theme, + Umang's 500 Liquid files). Har existing section/template ko type-wise categorize kare aur mark: REUSE (normalize) / DUPLICATE / JUNK / GAP. Output: "X existing → N reuse, M gaps to build." Tracker ki inventory table bhare. Why first: bahut variants already exist — duplicate labor mat karo.

Phase B — Gap analysis

Har section type ke liye: target variants vs existing reuse-able = kitne naye chahiye. Tracker update. Priority high-impact + product-focused sections pe (hero, product-card, product-grid, pdp, featured-grid).

Phase C — Prove the method on ONE section

Ek section lo (recommend: hero ya product-card). Uske gaps build karo + existing ko normalize karo, taaki uske 5-6 variants complete hon. Render-verify (Umang's eyes, real preview link). Confirm woh 5-6 genuinely alag feel dete hain, sirf alag nahi dikhte. Jab tak ye prove na ho, scale mat karo.

Phase D — Scale to all section types

Phase C ka pattern baaki 13 section types pe repeat. Har variant Definition-of-Done se guzre (token-driven, neutral data, responsive, render-verified). Tracker se progress track.

Phase E — Per-niche blueprints

Har niche ke liye ek recipe: section mix + palette family + copy/imagery tone + variant bias. Naya Liquid nahi — ek shared library, blueprints se niche-identity aati hai. 2-3 niches se shuru.

Phase F — Generation engine

Assembly logic banao:

Merchant ke catalog + niche input lo (products, images, count).
Blueprint pick karo → section types + variant pool decide.
Har slot ke liye variant randomly-but-coherently pick karo (aesthetic coherence rules — clashing combos avoid).
templates/*.json programmatically compose karo (section order + which sections).
Ek token set apply karo (color/font/radius layer).
Merchant ke apne products/images inject karo (live Liquid objects; missing-asset fallback).
CRO checklist run karo — fail hone wale section ko dusre variant se swap karo.
3 stores output do; reject hone pe naye 3 (unlimited, non-colliding).
Phase G — End-to-end test

Ek real merchant store pe poora flow chalao: niche → 3 stores → render-verify (responsive both devices) → CRO pass → merchant products live dikhe. Collision-check: do stores perceptibly alag hon.

Locked principles (har phase mein binding)
Structural variation, not cosmetic — variants layout-level alag, color-level token layer sambhalta hai.
Token-driven from the start — no hardcoded hex; text-on-colored-bg = #fff/--text-on-accent, not --surface.
Zero fabricated data — neutral defaults, trust signals default-hidden, merchant products live-pulled.
Adapt to merchant catalog — image/product availability ke hisaab se variant pick.
Responsive both devices — har variant mobile + desktop.
Prove small, then scale — ek section render-verified (Umang's eyes) before scaling.
CRO checklist = hygiene, not guaranteed conversion — real CRO live A/B se prove hota hai.
Reuse before build — existing codebase sections/templates pehle inventory + normalize.
Render-proof viewable — real preview link, local-path screenshot nahi; close Umang's eyes se.
